00:35:22.260 --> 00:35:24.687
Georgiana receives this
award for her thesis,

00:35:24.687 --> 00:35:28.340
"Support or Interference:
Relational Influences

00:35:28.340 --> 00:35:32.430
on Mothers' Exclusive
Breastfeeding Practices in Ghana."

00:35:32.430 --> 00:35:34.410
Childhood malnutrition is a challenge

00:35:34.410 --> 00:35:37.750
that needs to be understood
as a global health threat.

00:35:37.750 --> 00:35:41.620
Exclusive breastfeeding is
recognized as the best practice

00:35:41.620 --> 00:35:44.810
to improve a child's growth
and cognitive development

00:35:44.810 --> 00:35:46.810
in the first months of life.

00:35:46.810 --> 00:35:49.010
The World Health Organization recommends

00:35:49.010 --> 00:35:51.940
exclusive breastfeeding until six months.

00:35:51.940 --> 00:35:53.550
Mothers need family support

00:35:53.550 --> 00:35:56.460
to adhere to exclusive
breastfeeding practice.

00:35:56.460 --> 00:35:58.420
This study aimed to understand

00:35:58.420 --> 00:36:01.637
the interpersonal level
relational influences

00:36:03.120 --> 00:36:07.330
of fathers, grandmothers,
and other family members

00:36:07.330 --> 00:36:09.540
on the mother-child dyad adherence

00:36:09.540 --> 00:36:11.770
to exclusive breastfeeding practices,

00:36:11.770 --> 00:36:15.320
as well as document community
and societal influences

00:36:15.320 --> 00:36:17.240
on exclusive breastfeeding.

00:36:17.240 --> 00:36:20.334
Georgiana, please come
to receive your award.

00:36:20.334 --> 00:36:23.334
(audience cheering)

