00:39:50.230 --> 00:39:54.960
the first head of the YSPH
International Health Division.

00:39:54.960 --> 00:39:56.460
I'm very pleased to announce

00:39:56.460 --> 00:39:58.290
that the Lowell Levin Award for Excellence

00:39:58.290 --> 00:40:02.140
in Global Health has been awarded to...

00:40:02.140 --> 00:40:05.326
Are your ready again? Georgiana Esteves.

00:40:05.326 --> 00:40:08.326
(audience cheering)

00:40:15.070 --> 00:40:19.030
I'll try that pronunciation
again. Georgiana Esteves.

00:40:19.030 --> 00:40:23.020
Georgiana came to YSPH after
working with the Dara Institute

00:40:23.020 --> 00:40:26.470
in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, for five years.

00:40:26.470 --> 00:40:29.490
The Dara Institute is a
civil society organization

00:40:29.490 --> 00:40:32.480
that works to promote
health and human development

00:40:32.480 --> 00:40:34.250
by implementing and fostering

00:40:34.250 --> 00:40:36.780
an integrated approach to fight poverty.

00:40:36.780 --> 00:40:39.930
She's also a registered
nutritionist in Brazil

00:40:39.930 --> 00:40:42.980
and managed her private practice

00:40:42.980 --> 00:40:46.720
for seven years until
joining YSPH in 2020.

00:40:46.720 --> 00:40:49.280
Since her arrival, she's
been a very engaged student

00:40:49.280 --> 00:40:51.810
in the Department of Social
and Behavioral Sciences,

00:40:51.810 --> 00:40:54.150
pursuing the Global Health Concentration

00:40:54.150 --> 00:40:58.320
as well as the Maternal and
Child Health Promotion Track.

00:40:58.320 --> 00:40:59.990
Through her passion for global health

00:40:59.990 --> 00:41:02.310
and by leveraging her past experiences,

00:41:02.310 --> 00:41:03.590
she helped to facilitate

00:41:03.590 --> 00:41:05.900
a Global Health signature internship

00:41:05.900 --> 00:41:07.630
with the Dara Institute.

00:41:07.630 --> 00:41:09.960
As a result, a current
Global Health student

00:41:09.960 --> 00:41:12.280
will be working there this summer.

00:41:12.280 --> 00:41:14.430
Georgiana's academic performance

00:41:14.430 --> 00:41:16.810
in global health has been exceptional.

00:41:16.810 --> 00:41:18.870
Her thesis project is based on

00:41:18.870 --> 00:41:22.510
a highly innovative qualitative
analysis documenting

00:41:22.510 --> 00:41:25.500
the role that fathers can play
in supporting infant feeding

00:41:25.500 --> 00:41:28.800
and other caregiving practices
in Ghana, West Africa.

00:41:28.800 --> 00:41:31.500
Her influential work
is now informing UNICEF

00:41:31.500 --> 00:41:34.100
and other agencies on how to better design

00:41:34.100 --> 00:41:36.600
and implement effective infant feeding

00:41:36.600 --> 00:41:39.140
and maternal-child
health programs involving

00:41:39.140 --> 00:41:41.590
both adult and teenage fathers.

00:41:41.590 --> 00:41:44.776
Georgiana, please come
to receive your award.

00:41:44.776 --> 00:41:47.776
(audience cheering)

