01:39:36.830 --> 01:39:40.020
the YSPH students receiving their PhD

01:39:40.020 --> 01:39:42.010
and Master of Science degrees

01:39:42.010 --> 01:39:44.750
from the Graduate School
of Arts and Sciences.

01:39:44.750 --> 01:39:47.370
But they're really ours, don't you think?

01:39:47.370 --> 01:39:49.300
The 21 Doctoral graduates

01:39:49.300 --> 01:39:53.150
and 33 MS graduates are
listed in your program.

01:39:53.150 --> 01:39:54.900
And they're recognized more fully

01:39:54.900 --> 01:39:57.660
through Yale's Graduate
School Commencement events,

01:39:57.660 --> 01:39:59.520
which is where they are now.

01:39:59.520 --> 01:40:01.980
Please join me in recognizing all of them

01:40:01.980 --> 01:40:03.414
with a round of applause.

01:40:03.414 --> 01:40:06.414
(audience cheering)

01:40:15.620 --> 01:40:17.300
I immediately see that the dean's

01:40:17.300 --> 01:40:18.990
closing remarks are a little too long,

01:40:18.990 --> 01:40:22.290
but don't worry, we'll be there.

01:40:22.290 --> 01:40:24.500
We're seeing the light
at the end of the tunnel

01:40:24.500 --> 01:40:26.560
of this extraordinary day.

01:40:26.560 --> 01:40:28.420
As we approach the end of our ceremony,

01:40:28.420 --> 01:40:32.350
I address you, the YSPH Class of 2022.

01:40:32.350 --> 01:40:34.540
The degrees you've been
awarded today are a testament

01:40:34.540 --> 01:40:38.420
to your commitment to promoting
wellness in communities,

01:40:38.420 --> 01:40:42.110
promoting health equity, and
alleviating human suffering

01:40:42.110 --> 01:40:45.040
through the field of public health.

01:40:45.040 --> 01:40:48.290
The faculty and I salute
you for your perseverance,

01:40:48.290 --> 01:40:52.510
especially through the travails
of the COVID-19 pandemic.

01:40:52.510 --> 01:40:54.670
We also wish to thank, again,

01:40:54.670 --> 01:40:56.590
all the families and
friends of the graduates

01:40:56.590 --> 01:40:58.850
for joining us in this celebration.

01:40:58.850 --> 01:41:00.930
All of you in attendance,

01:41:00.930 --> 01:41:03.420
families, faculty, and staff alike,

01:41:03.420 --> 01:41:06.260
have encouraged and inspired
our students to succeed

01:41:06.260 --> 01:41:09.120
in this exciting stage
of their career studies.

01:41:09.120 --> 01:41:11.930
Yale University also wants to acknowledge

01:41:11.930 --> 01:41:15.210
that Indigenous Peoples
and Nations have stewarded

01:41:15.210 --> 01:41:18.610
through generations
the lands and waterways

01:41:18.610 --> 01:41:21.270
of what is now the state of Connecticut.

01:41:21.270 --> 01:41:23.700
We honor and respect the
enduring relationship

01:41:23.700 --> 01:41:28.470
that exists between these Peoples
and Nations and this land.

01:41:28.470 --> 01:41:31.460
Graduates, you're moving
on to your job searches,

01:41:31.460 --> 01:41:34.370
your new jobs, or your continuing doctoral

01:41:34.370 --> 01:41:36.090
or professional studies

01:41:36.090 --> 01:41:39.410
at a time of true crisis in
our nation and the world.

01:41:39.410 --> 01:41:42.180
Rather than facts, some would promote lies

01:41:42.180 --> 01:41:44.770
and so-called alternative facts.

01:41:44.770 --> 01:41:47.490
Rather than policy built
on an evidence base,

01:41:47.490 --> 01:41:49.990
some would promote partisan fictions

01:41:49.990 --> 01:41:52.240
for their own short-term gain.

01:41:52.240 --> 01:41:55.030
Rather than strengthening
fairness and democracy,

01:41:55.030 --> 01:41:57.950
some would roll back the
clock to restrict voting

01:41:57.950 --> 01:42:01.417
and biasing electoral processes.

01:42:01.417 --> 01:42:03.960
"America First" was the motto of Americans

01:42:03.960 --> 01:42:06.287
who were pro-Nazi in the 1930s.

01:42:06.287 --> 01:42:08.460
"America First" is now the motto

01:42:08.460 --> 01:42:11.430
for pro-authoritarian, pro-aggression,

01:42:11.430 --> 01:42:16.160
and racist and anti-immigrant
philosophies in the 2020s.

01:42:16.160 --> 01:42:20.020
What, then, are scientists to
do to help guide policymakers

01:42:20.020 --> 01:42:24.320
and sincerely motivated political leaders?

01:42:24.320 --> 01:42:25.940
I suggest three strategies.

01:42:25.940 --> 01:42:28.270
First, make every effort to take

01:42:28.270 --> 01:42:30.950
your peer-focused research publications

01:42:30.950 --> 01:42:33.150
and your professional presentations

01:42:33.150 --> 01:42:35.830
into a community context.

01:42:35.830 --> 01:42:39.090
This is easier than ever
with strong social media

01:42:39.090 --> 01:42:41.530
and online publication options.

01:42:41.530 --> 01:42:44.470
In this way, you will democratize science,

01:42:44.470 --> 01:42:47.250
bringing lay descriptions
of your work to persons

01:42:47.250 --> 01:42:49.460
who will never read it
in "Nature," "JAMA,"

01:42:49.460 --> 01:42:51.830
or the "American Journal
of Public Health."

01:42:51.830 --> 01:42:54.960
Second, seek to engage your local online

01:42:54.960 --> 01:42:57.550
or print newspapers with editorials,

01:42:57.550 --> 01:43:00.680
with commentaries to
counteract misinformation

01:43:00.680 --> 01:43:04.210
that is promulgated by
anti-science forces.

01:43:04.210 --> 01:43:07.580
Third, try your very best
to clarify scientific

01:43:07.580 --> 01:43:09.470
and social misinformation

01:43:09.470 --> 01:43:11.860
in your family and friendship groups,

01:43:11.860 --> 01:43:15.810
your local parent-teachers
associations and governments,

01:43:15.810 --> 01:43:19.510
and your fraternal organizations
and places of worship.

01:43:19.510 --> 01:43:21.530
Listen to alternative points of view,

01:43:21.530 --> 01:43:23.460
and seek to find common ground,

01:43:23.460 --> 01:43:26.500
but then address misinformation.

01:43:26.500 --> 01:43:28.840
Trust me, with your public
health degree in hand,

01:43:28.840 --> 01:43:30.890
your legitimacy will be enhanced

01:43:30.890 --> 01:43:33.483
and you can change hearts and minds.

01:43:34.440 --> 01:43:36.560
I would be remiss in not acknowledging

01:43:36.560 --> 01:43:39.680
the acute suffering of
our fellow human beings

01:43:39.680 --> 01:43:43.960
in such settings as Rohingya
or Syrian refugee camps,

01:43:43.960 --> 01:43:48.370
in Afghanistan and Yemen, in
the Tigray region of Ethiopia,

01:43:48.370 --> 01:43:50.960
and, most notably, in Ukraine.

01:43:50.960 --> 01:43:54.400
Less obvious at present is the growing

01:43:54.400 --> 01:43:56.860
climate change migration
of persons displaced

01:43:56.860 --> 01:44:01.120
by desertification, deforestation,
water and food shortages,

01:44:01.120 --> 01:44:03.960
and disturbed fisheries and agriculture.

01:44:03.960 --> 01:44:06.930
Also less obvious is the continuing crisis

01:44:06.930 --> 01:44:10.280
of suboptimal nutrition
and sedentary lifestyles,

01:44:10.280 --> 01:44:13.210
obstacles to healthy aging,

01:44:13.210 --> 01:44:15.870
inequities in access to health care,

01:44:15.870 --> 01:44:18.860
ongoing harmful substance use,

01:44:18.860 --> 01:44:21.900
links of suboptimal housing and health,

01:44:21.900 --> 01:44:26.320
systematic socioeconomic
disadvantages, infectious threats,

01:44:26.320 --> 01:44:28.750
and toxic environmental exposures.

01:44:28.750 --> 01:44:31.170
We can influence all these challenges,

01:44:31.170 --> 01:44:33.733
but we must make our science accessible.

01:44:34.600 --> 01:44:37.440
YSPH has made major
strides towards improving

01:44:37.440 --> 01:44:40.440
our communications to the
public and our policymakers.

01:44:40.440 --> 01:44:42.530
We intend to do much more.

01:44:42.530 --> 01:44:46.070
I invite you to stay in touch
with us and partner with us

01:44:46.070 --> 01:44:48.963
and the broader Yale community,
including our alumni.

01:44:51.052 --> 01:44:56.052
And we want to advocate towards
broad welfare of humanity,

01:44:56.640 --> 01:44:58.410
particularly those most vulnerable

01:44:58.410 --> 01:45:01.700
due to systematic economic
and housing discrimination

01:45:01.700 --> 01:45:03.470
that might lead to food deserts,

01:45:03.470 --> 01:45:06.900
risk of injury and violence,
educational disadvantages,

01:45:06.900 --> 01:45:10.290
and so many other
health-linked social issues.

01:45:10.290 --> 01:45:12.570
The good news is that in our profession,

01:45:12.570 --> 01:45:16.100
we spend our professional lives
working towards mitigation

01:45:16.100 --> 01:45:18.720
of these legacies of
structural disadvantage,

01:45:18.720 --> 01:45:21.500
health inequity, racial discrimination,

01:45:21.500 --> 01:45:23.800
and extreme economic disparities.

01:45:23.800 --> 01:45:26.640
We strive for improved health
systems and functioning.

01:45:26.640 --> 01:45:28.350
We seek cleaner environments

01:45:28.350 --> 01:45:31.740
and addressing the greenhouse
gas emissions crisis.

01:45:31.740 --> 01:45:35.540
We identify and mitigate the
social determinants of disease.

01:45:35.540 --> 01:45:39.980
We seek to motivate and
facilitate healthful behaviors.

01:45:39.980 --> 01:45:42.090
The personal and community antecedents

01:45:42.090 --> 01:45:43.800
of rising chronic diseases

01:45:43.800 --> 01:45:47.270
and ongoing infectious disease
threats are characterized

01:45:47.270 --> 01:45:50.550
and then interventions are
designed and promulgated.

01:45:50.550 --> 01:45:52.860
Importantly, the methods of public health

01:45:52.860 --> 01:45:55.660
in such disciplines as biostatistics,

01:45:55.660 --> 01:45:57.770
data sciences, health informatics,

01:45:57.770 --> 01:46:00.150
and implementation sciences are the source

01:46:00.150 --> 01:46:02.180
of discovery and innovation.

01:46:02.180 --> 01:46:04.650
Our global partnerships enable discovery

01:46:04.650 --> 01:46:07.760
and capacity-building in low
and middle-income countries

01:46:07.760 --> 01:46:11.700
and our students are in the
center of so much of this work.

01:46:11.700 --> 01:46:15.500
We are privileged to be in
the field of public health

01:46:15.500 --> 01:46:18.690
and your faculty are pleased to honor you

01:46:18.690 --> 01:46:21.660
on this day of your achievements.

01:46:21.660 --> 01:46:23.620
Finally, thank you most sincerely

01:46:23.620 --> 01:46:26.330
to our Student Affairs team
that I mentioned a moment ago.

01:46:26.330 --> 01:46:27.870
They've worked so hard.

01:46:27.870 --> 01:46:31.330
Dean Grosso, Registrar Stacey Tuttle,

01:46:31.330 --> 01:46:34.440
alongside my own colleagues
in the Office of the Dean.

01:46:34.440 --> 01:46:37.000
They've supported you
for the past few years,

01:46:37.000 --> 01:46:39.010
starting during the application process

01:46:39.010 --> 01:46:41.840
and throughout your
graduate experience at Yale.

01:46:41.840 --> 01:46:44.050
Please join me in thanking them

01:46:44.050 --> 01:46:45.040
for everything they've done

01:46:45.040 --> 01:46:46.980
throughout your graduate training

01:46:46.980 --> 01:46:48.486
at the Yale School of Public Health.

01:46:48.486 --> 01:46:51.653
(audience applauding)

01:46:57.410 --> 01:47:02.410
Please stay in touch with your
old teachers and the AYAPH,

01:47:02.760 --> 01:47:05.790
our Association for Yale
Alumni in Public Health,

01:47:05.790 --> 01:47:08.020
in which you are now subscribed.

01:47:08.020 --> 01:47:10.980
Let us know about the work
you do, your successes,

01:47:10.980 --> 01:47:13.750
and your willingness to
advise current students,

01:47:13.750 --> 01:47:16.830
mentor them, to receive
future summer interns,

01:47:16.830 --> 01:47:19.040
in the positions you
now find yourselves in,

01:47:19.040 --> 01:47:21.820
and to contribute to
the Annual Alumni Fund

01:47:21.820 --> 01:47:24.220
for their scholarships in the future.

01:47:24.220 --> 01:47:27.490
We will always value your
advice and your support.

01:47:27.490 --> 01:47:30.500
And a personal thank you to
students, staff, and faculty

01:47:30.500 --> 01:47:33.700
for their support of my
five-year tenure as your dean.

01:47:33.700 --> 01:47:37.520
This concludes the YSPH Diploma Ceremony.

01:47:37.520 --> 01:47:39.820
We ask that guests remain in their seats

01:47:39.820 --> 01:47:42.863
until the representing
faculty members have departed.

01:47:43.775 --> 01:47:46.775
(audience cheering)

